            <ArticleTitle>Total Synthesis of Neodysiherbaine A via 1,3-Dipolar Cycloaddition of a Chiral Nitrone Template.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6320-6323</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03092</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The total synthesis of neodysiherbaine A was achieved via 1,3-dipolar cycloaddition of a chiral nitrone template with a sugar-derived allyl alcohol in the presence of MgBr2·OEt2. This cycloaddition constructed the C2 and C4 asymmetric centers in a single step. Then reductive cleavage, intramolecular SN2 reaction of the tertiary alcohol, and oxidation of the primary alcohol afforded neodysiherbaine A.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
